<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jassim bin Muhammad Al Thani</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1825–<a href="/years/1913">1913</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Sheikh Jassim</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jassim bin Muhammad <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-thani">Al Thani</a> was ruler of Qatar from 1878 to 1913 and is regarded as the founder of the modern state. Balancing between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, he defeated an Ottoman force at the Battle of al-Wajbah in 1893, confirming his family's authority over the peninsula. Qatar's National Day, 18 December, marks his accession.</p></div>
